{"title":"2007 SMT Team Round Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_SMT_Team_Round_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are each randomly and independently chosen in the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/c/1fc72dd78dccabfb5e8493e08d925fb23d3286e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[-1, 1],$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> what is the probability\nthat <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/c/6cc051eb8520e261930a40604c91ddf03f2319d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a| + |b| &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_SMT_Team_Round_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To solve this, let's draw an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef870ce9fefe09b80a97b05a7b9198414c1b35f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />-plane and have both the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />-axis and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />-axis go from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and have the origin by at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/1/a11af309f4f98a632b52d2972cd9de92053c603c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1,-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" />. Let's now find the places where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/2/632b567423811830630b49e638a8ebe485c7c816.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a|+|b|=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" />. We have that at the lines: one at the upper right corner, one at the lower right corner, one at the upper left corner, and one at the lower left corner, and each of them cuts out an isosceles triangle with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. All of these isosceles triangles are regions where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/8/d88993dc9586b7bec44c7c8a6d94d2705662de13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a|+|b|&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" /> (you can test some values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> to see if you want), so out of the full square with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/9/4697867ef2cfc747a165d582f3fd4f07a157eb2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\times2=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"12\" />, an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/a/72a3958a97b16d09ad2b67c4d1f24c148b5559b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\times\\left(\\dfrac{1\\times1}2\\right)=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"137\" height=\"45\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/8/d88993dc9586b7bec44c7c8a6d94d2705662de13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a|+|b|&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" />, so an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> would be the region where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/1/671c69d503b80be089d816153692e461a21a9cc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a|+|b|&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore, our desired probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/d/c6db09ead7f628a56b48d03bfc0a8222841bfffc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\dfrac12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"26\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~Yuhao2012\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018053530\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.022 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 73/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3559/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37141:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018053530 and revision id 286873. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}